// The package, as one name.
//
// **Nothing like this exists today, and I got the reason wrong once.** `import { Read } from "core";`
// works, and the spec calls `core` *"the root of the tree"*, which I read as the root aggregating
// every file's exports. It does not. Measured: `Read` is the only name that crosses, and
// `Result`, `Option`, `Map` and `hashBytes` are all refused from `"core"` with
//
//     = help: import it from the file that declares it — importing does not re-export
//
// So `"core"` names one file and there is no aggregation anywhere. Re-export does not exist at all,
// which is exactly what `packages/fmt`'s header says and what `wac-mono 0072` is open about.
//
// That makes an explicit barrel the only proposal on the table rather than the better of two, and
// it is still the one worth having, for a reason aggregation would not have given: **the list is a
// judgement.** `export` marks what leaves a *file*; a barrel marks what leaves a *package*. Without
// the second level a helper two files share has to be public, and `packages/http`'s `findCrlf` is
// what that costs — duplicated between two files rather than shared, because its header says
// *"neither wanted to export a helper the other would then depend on."* A duplicate chosen over a
// leak.

export { Result } from "./result.wac";
export { Vec } from "./vec.wac";
export { Map } from "./map.wac";
export { Queue } from "./queue.wac";
export { Slice, Bytes } from "./slice.wac";
export { Ticket, TicketBase, Continuation, Circular, Stuck, all, any } from "./ticket.wac";
export { Coroutine, Generator, AsyncGenerator, Step } from "./coroutine.wac";
